<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Brownies (Grandma Genevieve)</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell>1 stick butter</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 cups sugar</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>4 eggs</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell>4 ounces unsweetened chocolate melted and cooled</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 teaspoons vanilla</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>1 \frac{1}{2}</m> cups flour</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cup milk</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>1 \frac{1}{2}</m> cups walnuts (optional)</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Cream the butter and sugar.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add the eggs and beat until smooth.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add the chocolate, vanilla, flour, &amp; milk, and mix it all together.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Stir in walnuts, if desired.  Bake at <m>325^\circ</m> for 30 minutes in a 9" x 13" pan, because what kind of dummy would try baking it in a 9" x 9" inch pan?
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          These brownies are really good, and super cake-y.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>